{
 "why": {
  "response": "A case of the plan's server responses. It covers one response of the contract, named by its operation and status, such as API-131#403, and reaches its requirements through that operation in stage 06.",
  "outcome": "A case of the plan's hub command outcomes. It covers one outcome of a hub command, named by the command's API ID, and reaches its requirements through that command in stage 06.",
  "state": "A case of the plan's screen states. It covers one state of a screen, such as SCR-101#error, with the responses or the data that lead to it, and reaches its requirements through the screen in stage 07 and the responses in stage 06.",
  "example": "A case of 0.2.1's endpoint-specific examples. It covers one example response of the contract by its operation and status, as the server responses do.",
  "memory": "An ID of the memory part, which kodonghui/corthex defines. Stages 01 and 03 name memory's terms and contexts beside a word of NEXUS that means the same or differs, and stages 01, 03 and 04 say that their own numbers start after memory's.",
  "files": "A file of the hub, the snapshot, the stage records, the status file, the outbox or the session reads (TBL-114 to TBL-117, TBL-125), or a table that phase ② plans (TBL-118 to TBL-124). The ERD guide defines them in its table of records beside nexus.sql, and the hub reads nexus.sql alone as stage 05's source.",
  "sample": "An ID of an example or of a synthetic fixture: the contract's table of the forms that a source takes, and results that name their fixture's items, kept as written.",
  "bug": "A bug that an earlier run found. The plan's evidence names it in its text and in tables whose first column is headed Bug, which the hub reads as mentions; the plan has no table of bugs with an ID column."
